# Exact edge-bias review

Disposition: the supplied two-qubit triple provides a computable strong spectral point and arbitrarily small strong positive biases. I found no load-bearing algebraic defect in the candidate. It supplies the strong-point input to the previously qualified conditional static-bias transfer **only if the positive anisotropic terms on the existing old edge can actually be installed, attenuated and calibrated**. That permission is stronger than the original first-site-only control domain. This result does not invalidate the earlier onsite-bias obstruction, supply the remaining controller hardware, prove a generic Lie-certificate implication, or confer retained/audit status.

This review contains an independently reconstructed equation-level calculation sealed before candidate access, followed by source-exposed comparison. The parent supplied both the equations and the purpose of finding an escape from the onsite obstruction. The same model and effort were retained. There is no claim of independent example selection, blind task framing, or model-family replication.

